    "summary": "Acoustic gems & fiery New Speedway Boogie dominate the show",
    "blurb": "The first set delivers a string of acoustic highlights—Deep Elem Blues, Me & My Uncle and Mama Tried—while the second set erupts with a scorching New Speedway Boogie and tight electric jams. Jerry’s guitar shines both unplugged and on the high‑energy boogie, and The Other One rolls out a solid improvisational stretch.",
    "review": "May 1, 1970 at Alfred College captured one of the Grateful Dead’s most celebrated early‑70 shows. An almost flawless acoustic first set unfolds with tight renditions of Deep Elem Blues, Monkey And The Engineer, Me & My Uncle* and Mama Tried*, each showcasing Garcia’s pristine tone and a lyrical extra on I Know You Rider despite a bit of mic‑noise. The band then pivots into electric fireworks – New Speedway Boogie roars forward as Jerry trades scorching licks with Bob, while The Race Is On* and Wake Up Little Susie* keep the momentum high. The second set builds into a classic The Other One sandwich with a powerful drum break, and finishes with a soulful turn on Turn On Your Lovelight. Across all four soundboard sources the performance is consistently praised; the Miller SBD (gd1970-05-01.sbd.miller.95683.sbeok.flac16) stands out for its crisp stereo image and full‑show coverage, making it the go‑to source for reliving this historic night.",
